# Web & Admin - Next.js + TypeScript

## Stack
- Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Hosting is the project owner's choice; the `deployment` skill (`.agents/skills/deployment/SKILL.md`) has a Cloudflare Workers via OpenNext example
- Fetch-based API helpers and NextAuth route handlers

## Structure (web-user-app/ and web-admin-portal/)
```
app/                -> App Router pages, layouts, and route handlers
components/         -> Reusable UI and layout components
lib/api/            -> Fetch helpers for `/api/v1`
lib/auth/           -> Backend session cookie and sign-out helpers
lib/config/         -> Route and runtime config helpers
types/              -> NextAuth and other shared TypeScript types
auth.ts             -> NextAuth configuration
middleware.ts       -> Locale/auth middleware when present
```

## Admin Additions
- Sidebar shell (`components/layout/admin-shell.tsx`) with navigation
- Starter tables and cards under `app/admin/(dashboard)/` to replace with product screens
- Admin role guard: the dashboard layout redirects to `/admin/login` unless the session role is `ADMIN`

## Patterns
- Server Components by default, `"use client"` only when needed
- Auth: NextAuth route handlers with OAuth and/or credentials
- API calls proxy through `/api/v1/[...path]` with `fetch`; the proxy forwards only plain paths under `/api/v1/`
- Sign-out goes through `signOutEverywhere` (`lib/auth/sign-out.ts`): it revokes the backend refresh session, then Auth.js clears the web session
- Keep secrets out of the repository; the project owner sets them in the chosen host
- Tailwind for styling and shared design patterns

## Commands
- `npm run dev` or `task web-user-app:dev`
- `npm run build` or `task web-user-app:build`
- `task web-admin-portal:dev`
- `task web-admin-portal:build`
